<title>AUSTRALIA: WMC AWARDS LURGI ACID PLANT CONTRACT.</title>
<headline>WMC AWARDS LURGI ACID PLANT CONTRACT.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold and base metals miner WMC Ltd said on Wednesday it had awarded Lurgi Pty Ltd, a unit of Metallgesellschaft AG (MG), the contract to build a one million tonne per annum sulphuric acid plant in Queensland.</p>
<p>&quot;In Queensland we have today awarded the one million tonne per annum sulphuric acid plant construction contract to Lurgi for the High Analysis Fertiliser project,&quot; WMC said in a statement announcing its annual results.  </p>
<p>During its year ended June 30, WMC committed to construction of the A$650 million High Analysis Fertiliser project, with facilities at Phosphate Hill, Mt Isa and Townsville.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
